  "body": "Found by a reviewer's trial merge on origin/main 5bdfc00c, an hour after 41 PRs merged (each was tested alone, never together). The batch gate on 09720ae3 is still running and may add to this list; anything it adds is commented here.\n\n**1. `camcraft-app` lib tests do not compile.** `crates/app/src/operation/rotary_law_tests.rs:27` builds a `Cutter` without the `neck` field. PR #957 (merged as 23038434) added `Cutter::neck`; PR #1064 (merged as 27b5e040) added this test file against the old struct. The app itself builds; `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib` does not. Check every other hand-built `Cutter { .. }` (and `VerifyContext { .. }`) in tests that came in with today's merges.\n\n**2. `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_tormach_plasma`: 8 recorded refusals are stale.** PR #1002 (merged as 599b78a7) recorded the plasma post's refusal with the old wording (\"no machine is not declared a plasma machine\"); PR #1049 (merged as 6464dda0, for #998) changed that sentence. The recorded `.refusal` files under `crates/post/tests/recorded/` need the new sentence; nothing else in them may move.\n\nWhy P1 and not P0: both are test-side breaks (a fixture missing a field, recorded text behind a wording fix); no posted program or check is wrong. They block every gate on main, so this goes first.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib` compiles and passes; `cargo test -p camcraft-post` passes with the recorded refusals differing from before ONLY by the new sentence (the PR shows the diff of one file as an example and states the count); `cargo xtask gate batch` on the fixed tree is green, or whatever else is red is listed here with the merge that caused it.\n",
